{
  "summary": "Audited steering-doc.md against evidence.md and the live repo. Re-verified all checkable external/repo facts directly (repo inventory, git remote/log, .gitignore, installed pi-coding-agent/agent-browser versions, ~/.pi/agent/settings.json packages field, CreateAgentSessionOptions field names, Electron docs quotes, console-message fields, etc.) — all held up. Focused the contract-conformance check on: (1) every invariant in Shape/Done-looks-like/Behaviour-table tracing to a Decision's `*Enforced:*` line, (2) every Decision's named choke point appearing by that name in Shape or Contracts, (3) `## Not doing` vs contradicting Decisions, (4) Zone B introducing no decisions absent from Zone A. Found 4 blocking issues: an \"empty prompt\" Behaviour-table row citing D3 for a rule D3's text never states; a reload/close/quit session-disposal claim (in Shape, Contracts, and two Behaviour-table rows) tagged D6 but never established in D6's own decision text; log-durability claims (synchronous writes, drop-not-buffer) tagged D9 but absent from D9's text; and a Contracts preload constraint (\"no require outside electron\") that directly contradicts the document's own Facts-on-file line (which correctly lists electron/events/timers/url as permitted). Found 4 minor issues: D1 carries the ⚠ flag but is omitted from \"Where to push back\"; D3's prose omits \"thinking\" events from its drop list even though the mapping table and evidence support dropping them; prove:sdk's 60-second timeout appears only in Contracts with no Zone A backing; and \"Both flavors are agent-drivable\" in the Glossary delta reads oddly next to the document's zero-cost framing. Wrote full findings with quotes and locations to fact-audit-3.md.",
  "verdict": "{\"blocking\": [\"B1 — Behaviour table row \\\"Empty or whitespace-only prompt\\\" (Zone B, Behaviour and edge cases) is tagged D3, but D3's Decision text (## Decisions, D3) only covers the four-event vocabulary and which SDK events toPortEvent drops — it says nothing about prompt validation or admission. The invariant does not trace to a Decision that classifies it on an *Enforced:* line, contradicting evidence.md's own claim that D3's text 'establishes exactly that rule.'\", \"B2 — The claim that a window reload/close or app quit disposes the SDK adapter's in-flight session and releases the single-flight guard appears in Shape (Agent channel entry), Contracts (SDK adapter section), and two Behaviour-table rows ('Window reloads mid-turn', 'Window closed or app quits mid-turn'), all tagged D6 — but D6's own Decision text is entirely about single-flight refusal/turn-id correlation and never mentions window lifecycle, reload, close, or quit disposal. This consequential design commitment (whether a potentially paid session is torn down vs left running) is asserted as settled without ever being decided in the Decisions section — decision leakage.\", \"B3 — Behaviour table rows 'Log write fails mid-session' ('records are dropped, not buffered') and 'App quits with records in flight' ('append writes synchronously... no exit-time buffer') are both tagged D9, but D9's Decision text says only that append(record) writes one file per launch — nothing about synchronous I/O or a drop-not-buffer failure policy. These are real engineering commitments (blocking I/O on every log call; accepting silent data loss on write failure) introduced with no antecedent Decision or Enforced-line classification.\", \"B4 — Contracts states the preload 'must' have 'no require of anything outside electron' to load under the sandbox, but the same document's Facts on file section (sourced from evidence.md's reading of Electron's sandbox.md) correctly states a sandboxed preload may require electron, events, timers, AND url. Contracts misstates Electron's actual constraint within the same document that states it correctly elsewhere — a builder reading only Contracts would wrongly avoid requiring events/timers/url in the preload.\"], \"minor\": [\"M1 — D1 carries the '⚠' flag (shared only with D2, D3) but is never mentioned in the 'Where to push back' section, which discusses D2, D3, and A1 and then claims 'nothing else is blocked' — an inconsistency in the document's own flagging convention.\", \"M2 — D3's Decision text lists only 'tool, compaction and retry events' as dropped by the mapping, omitting 'thinking' events, even though the Behaviour table row and the toPortEvent mapping table (and the evidenced AssistantMessageEvent union) correctly treat thinking events as dropped too — the behavior is right, D3's own enumeration is incomplete.\", \"M3 — Contracts' prove:sdk pass criterion adds a specific 'within 60 seconds' timeout that appears nowhere in D12's Decision text or elsewhere in Zone A — a minor, low-stakes undecided implementation parameter.\", \"M4 — Glossary delta's Launch flavor entry says 'Both flavors are agent-drivable,' which reads oddly next to the document's repeated zero-cost-for-agents framing (dev:sdk costs money per the Launch flavors table); defensible per D5's own wording but worth a phrasing pass.\"]}"
}
